  "__________ offers neutrality (international arbitration allows each party to avoid the domestic courts of the other) and ease of enforcement (foreign awards can be easier to enforce than foreign court decisions).\nA. Buyer\nB. Seller\nC. The Bank\nD. Arbitration\nD",
  "__________ is a set of uniform rules codifying the interpretation of trade terms defining the rights and obligations of buyers and sellers in international transactions. It is developed and issued by the International Chamber of Commerce (ICC) in Paris.\nA. Incoterms\nB. URC\nC. UCP\nD. None of these\nA",
